<!-- The Kettenblatt mark for themed icons: the same chainring, drawn in code in the same spirit as
     map/Markers.kt. Five circles and two rings, no bitmap.

     The design spec's 100-unit geometry, scaled by 0.6061 into the 108dp
     adaptive canvas. That puts the outer teeth at a diameter of 60 within the
     72dp a launcher mask actually shows — Material's keyline for a circular
     mark. Sizing it to the 66dp safe circle instead left the teeth all but
     touching the mask edge, which read as cramped and turned the icon into a
     dark blob at launcher size.

     The spider holes and the bore are punched out with evenOdd rather than
     filled with the background colour, so the same paths work as a themed
     monochrome icon, where the system tints every opaque pixel. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Teeth: a dashed ring in the spec; VectorDrawable has no dash array, so
         the 24 teeth are drawn as 24 arcs at 15 degree spacing. -->
